Public specification:
The following is the state transition table for a Moore state machine with one input, one output, and four states. Implement this state machine. Include a synchronous active high reset that resets the FSM to state A. 
// State | Next state in=0, Next state in=1 | Output
// A | A, B | 0
// B | C, B | 0
// C | A, D | 0
// D | C, B | 1

Public interface: input widths {'in': 1, 'reset': 1}; output widths {'out': 1}.
Frozen timing: Clock clk; driven input row before the posedge sample, sampled after that edge settles. Optional mid changes inputs after this sample, before the other edge. The next row drives new inputs before the next sample.
Work independently from this public spec. Write concise concrete directed scenarios as JSON, with no executable model and no reasoning prose. A scenario starts at power-up; make reset/initialization explicit when possible. Cover reset and release where present, control combinations and precedence, width and value boundaries and all specified behaviors. Keep each scene <=20 cycles and all scenes <=120. Typical suite: 4–7 short scenes. Use a short exact verbatim spec substring per scene. Format: {"scenes":[{"id":"s1","spec_quote":"exact text","covers":["behavior","boundary"],"cycles":[{"in":{input:integer},optional "mid":{input:integer},"out":{output:integer}}]}]}. Write bit patterns as unsigned integer values.
Use brief private deliberation. Prioritize the complete artifact before the token limit.

